    "items": [
      {
        "text": "Pilar Schiavo has represented California's 40th Assembly District since 2022. She chairs the Assembly Committee on Military and Veterans Affairs and serves on the Health, Budget, and Utilities and Energy committees. Her campaign says she was a small business owner and nurse advocate who worked in the labor movement for over 20 years.",
        "cites": [1, 2, 3],
        "sentences": [
          {
            "text": "Pilar Schiavo has represented California's 40th Assembly District since 2022.",
            "cites": [1]
          },
          {
            "text": "She chairs the Assembly Committee on Military and Veterans Affairs and serves on the Health, Budget, and Utilities and Energy committees.",
            "cites": [2]
          },
          {
            "text": "Her campaign says she was a small business owner and nurse advocate who worked in the labor movement for over 20 years.",
            "cites": [3]
          }
        ]
      },
      {
        "text": "She says her 2026 legislation focuses on lowering costs, consumer protections, public safety, housing, and public health. She authored AB 1820, a law preventing added permit fees for electric vehicle chargers at apartment buildings. She says she helped secure $197 million for Medi-Cal eligibility workers and $50 million for crime victim services. She says residents suffer from toxic air from the underground fire at Chiquita Canyon Landfill.",
        "cites": [4, 5, 6, 7],
